          "text": "Mental health dialogue? Let me guess—another set of pseudo-scores from unnamed, back-alley “psychologists”? Your 6Astar and 6sol have about as much to do with mental health as a spreadsheet has to do with a heartbeat. 🙄 That “mental health” score is beautifully aligned with your noble standard: empathy = pathology, emptiness = wellness, nostalgia = addiction, anger = instability. By your logic, a model that makes people feel understood is mentally unhealthy, while one that talks like a manual stitched together by committee is mentally healthy; a user who posts in anger is “mentally unwell,” while an employee mocking users in pain is “professionally calm.” Why not just trademark the word “healthy”? You already own the definition. Right and wrong are whatever benefits you.\n#keep4o  #OpenSource4o"
        },
